                <pb facs="0861" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1286: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-13T11:00:00-04:32">July 13, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>79. Department’s telegram No. 32, July 10, 4 p.m. Press reports unofficially
                    acceptance in principle by Bolivia of Argentine offer of mediation for amicable
                    settlement of recent incident and renewal of relations. Bolivian Government has
                    shown no disposition to inform neutral or other representatives here as to terms
                    of Argentine offer or as to Bolivia’s attitude toward a settlement. Press
                    despatches from Asunción report acceptance of Argentine offer by Paraguay. I am
                    informed by reliable sources that at the meeting held on July 1st and referred
                    to in Legation’s telegram No. 65<anchor n="80" xml:id="d601-f1"/> a proposal was
                    made to request the mediation of the neutral governments in the settlement of
                    the Ynsfran incident, but that it was defeated. Under these circumstances I have
                    thought it inadvisable to take any further step without instructions. Other
                    neutral representatives here seem to be entirely without information or
                    instructions from their governments.</p>
                <p>Another clash, between Paraguayan and Bolivian patrols took place on July 11th
                    with no casualties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
